      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A guarding inspection is one of the most important checks in a factory. It is also easy to fudge. A defeated interlock, a missing guard or an emergency stop that does not latch are the faults that matter. Write the record at the machine, not later.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Machine inspection duties come from PUWER 1998, under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974.</li><li>The guarding ranking runs from fixed enclosing guards, to interlocked guards, to other devices, to appliances and information. Use the highest practical measure first.</li><li>A guarding inspection covers guards, interlocks, stops and emergency stops, trapping points, access, marks and isolation.</li><li>New machinery needs the right conformity marking. Check the current rules.</li><li>Quickler records what you found. It does not replace a competent person's examination.</li></ul>"
